; ============================================================
; GETSTR-Test  —  demo/verify the $C2 GETSTR line-input opcode
; ============================================================
; Needs Firmware-Math/GETSTR-2frag.dlines.txt flashed.
;
;   11 01 09 00   R1 = $0900   cursor      (-> $4900)
;   11 02 09 00   R2 = $0900   buffer start / backspace floor
;   C2 12         GETSTR: read a line into the buffer at R1, floor R2
;   C1 02         PRINTSTR the buffer back from R2
;
; Prompts "Type a line: ", reads what you type, then echoes "You typed: <line>".
;
; What to try:
;   plain text + Enter      -> the same text comes back
;   type, BACKSPACE, retype -> the erased characters are gone from the buffer
;                              and the screen shows BS SPACE BS (a real erase)
;   DEL instead of BACKSPACE-> behaves identically ($7F is an alias for $08)
;   BACKSPACE at the very start -> ignored; it will not eat the prompt
;   Enter on an empty line   -> "You typed: " with nothing after it
;
; GETSTR handles ONE character per execution and yields between them, so other
; VMs keep running while this one waits for you. It is not a blocking loop.
;
; NOTE: the strings live PAST the F0 00 00 end marker, so the label pre-pass
; never scans them - otherwise a stray $B3 byte in text reads as a label.
; ============================================================

; ---- CODE ($4000..$402B) ----
D 4000 CD
D 4001 11 03 09 40
D 4005 C1 03
D 4007 11 01 09 00
D 400B 11 02 09 00
D 400F C2 12
D 4011 10 00 0D C9
D 4015 10 00 0A C9
D 4019 11 03 09 20
D 401D C1 03
D 401F C1 02
D 4021 10 00 0D C9
D 4025 10 00 0A C9
D 4029 F0 00 00

; ---- strings, past the end marker ----
D 4920 59 6F 75 20 74 79 70 65 64 3A 20 00
D 4940 54 79 70 65 20 61 20 6C 69 6E 65 3A 20 00
D 5000 00
D 6000 00
D 7000 00
